2026-11-06T03:13:42.7697895Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7707010Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7707475Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7707952Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7708246Z 
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7708466Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7708761Z 
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7709016Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7709542Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7709835Z 
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7709968Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7710354Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7710918Z 
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7711296Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:13:42.7711781Z   $ sh ./install-nix
